1. Build Phase

This phase is about taking source code → producing a runnable artifact (image).
It happens inside Jenkins after GitHub push.

Backend (Spring Boot)

Checkout Code – Jenkins pulls latest code from GitHub.

Build JAR – mvn clean install compiles Java and produces a .jar.

Build Docker Image – Jenkins uses the repo’s Dockerfile to create an image:

docker build -t backend:<branch> .


<branch> → dev, stag, etc.

Frontend (Angular)

Checkout Code – Jenkins pulls Angular code.

Install Dependencies – npm install.

Build Angular App – ng build creates dist/ folder.

Build Docker Image (if you create one for Nginx) or prepare files for deployment.

✅ End of Build Phase:

Backend → Docker image with Spring Boot JAR.

Frontend → Angular build ready (inside Docker image or copied to server).

🔹 2. Deployment Phase

This phase is about running the new version of the app in UAT server.

Backend

Stop Old Container – docker-compose automatically replaces it.

Deploy New Container:

docker compose -f docker-compose.yaml up -d --no-deps backend-service


Uses the new backend image built in Build Phase.

Frontend

Deploy with External Compose File:

docker compose -f /home/docker-compose/frontend-container.yaml up -d --no-deps frontend-service


Only the frontend-service is restarted.

Other 20 apps in the YAML remain untouched.

✅ End of Deployment Phase:

Old containers are replaced with new ones.

UAT Dev/Staging servers now run the updated code.